                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "While this game might have been inspired from several sources it unfortunately comes off as a game that could have been better; more style over substance.\n\nFirst off I enjoy the graphics. It took a while to get used to the oddly proportioned characters but there isn’t many games that has this weird look. The gameplay is very run of the mill, with not much else that stands out. The gunplay comes off as generic and aside from the few things that you can use in the background such as road signs to split your shots to hit multiple targets there really isn't anything else of note. There are driving sections which sometimes go on for way too long. Stealth sections which are just bland and boring adding nothing else to the repetitiveness. Now don't get me wrong I don't mind repetitiveness but jesus most of the time gunplay feels unsatisfying no matter what weapon you use, handgun, revolver, smg none of them feel good to use.\n\nThe story only hits a high note at a single point in the game which I won't spoil here. But that's it. After that its a typical revenge story with characters who have zero presence until it is time to fight them in a boss battle. Dialogue is predictable, and the soundtrack is forgettable.\n\nThere are multiple endings but god if you think I'm going play that last section again you're mistaken.\n\nI got this when it was on sale but even there I feel cheated. You're better off spending your money somewhere else.",
